-- title:
--   An approximate factorization $d\approx s^*vs$ transports the hereditary subalgebra of $(d-\varepsilon)_+$ into that of $v$
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a possibly non-unital C$^*$-algebra, ordered by its positive cone. For $h\in A$ write
--   $$\operatorname{Her}(h)=\overline{\{\,h\,x\,h^{*}\ :\ x\in A\,\}}$$
--   for the norm closure of the set of sandwiches $hxh^*$. It is a closed $*$-subalgebra of $A$, and for positive $h$ it is the hereditary C$^*$-subalgebra generated by $h$. For positive $d$ and $\varepsilon>0$ let $(d-\varepsilon)_+=f(d)$ with $f(t)=\max(t-\varepsilon,0)$, defined by continuous functional calculus.
--
--   A *regular transport* from $h$ to $v$ (for $h,v\in A$) is a pair $(C,\Phi)$. Here $C:\operatorname{Her}(h)\to A$ is a bounded $\mathbb{C}$-linear map and $\Phi:\operatorname{Her}(h)\to A$ is a (not necessarily unital) $*$-homomorphism, such that for all $k,l\in\operatorname{Her}(h)$
--   $$C(k)^*C(l)=k^*l,\qquad C(k)\,C(l)^*=\Phi(k\,l^*),\qquad C(kl)=C(k)\,l,\qquad \Phi(k)\in\operatorname{Her}(v).$$
--   Heuristically $C(k)=wk$ and $\Phi(k)=wkw^*$ for a partial isometry $w$ whose source projection acts as a unit on $\operatorname{Her}(h)$. The axioms imply that $\Phi$ is isometric, so $\Phi$ identifies $\operatorname{Her}(h)$ with a C$^*$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{Her}(v)$.
--
--   **Theorem.** Let $d,v\in A$ be positive, $\varepsilon>0$, and $s\in A$ with
--   $$\|d-s^*vs\|<\varepsilon .$$
--   Then there exists a regular transport from $(d-\varepsilon)_+$ to $v$.
--
--   This is a hereditary-subalgebra form of the cut-down lemma of Cuntz comparison theory. Approximately dominating $d$ by $v$ up to $\varepsilon$ yields an exact embedding of the hereditary subalgebra of the $\varepsilon$-cut-down of $d$ into the hereditary subalgebra of $v$. In the proof of strong pure infiniteness it turns the approximate comparisons supplied by proper infiniteness into exact copies of hereditary subalgebras.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `RegularTransport (cut d ε) v` is a structure carrying data (`carrier` is $C$, `hom` is $\Phi$), so the theorem asserts that this type is `Nonempty`. Here `cut d ε = cfcₙ (fun t => max (t - ε) 0) d`, and the order on $A$ is any partial order making $A$ a star-ordered ring, which is necessarily the positive-cone order.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/PureInfiniteness/Hereditary.lean#L559-L605

